t story to tell and it  would give lots of opportunities for um  conversations about things that you know  you would want to organically bring up  with small with small people  what's it like to hear yourself bring an  animated character to life is it easier  to watch an animated movie that you've  done than when you do live action  it's so much easier to watch an animated  movie because you're not having to look  at your own face  although sometimes i you know listening  to myself when i have to go back and  listen to interviews is not always fun  so  i'm with you all the way i don't think  there's anybody that likes listening to  their voice or seeing their face  personally i mean maybe i'm wrong but i  think  it's always challenging  what was it like to get to sing a little  song for this too is that fun was it  exciting was it scary  so terrifying and i begged harry and  claire knight i said please please can't  somebody else sing this song it  shouldn't be me i can't sing i'm gonna  ruin the movie and they said please isla  and so i had to record it and  some members of the family that will  remain unnamed laughed very hard at my  rehearsal process uh but i tried to  remain courageous like maddie and i  recorded it and then when i heard it  actually in the movie i thought oh  you can't really tell it sounds fine  i love that each of these characters  have their own quirks and and their own  insecurities  personally do you feel most like maddie  or do you think you're more like any one  of the other characters  um i think growing up as a redhead in  australia with an english accent um i  definitely felt like adolescence was you  know i think you know in the same way  that maddie is sort of um  well you know maddie sort of  doesn't sort of you know it's hard for  her to accept her differences at the  beginning you know because obviously she  has  you know she was conditioned to believe  that she was this horrible thing and  then really she grows to learn to love 